= Interoperability — Technical =

Interoperability can be analyzed at transport, protocol, data-format, schema, semantic, identity, security, and operational layers. Conformance to a common specification reduces ambiguity but real interoperability still requires compatible profiles, versions, and deployment choices.

== Modeling / implementation cautions ==
* interoperability ≠ identical implementation
* data exchange ≠ semantic interoperability automatically
* shared standard ≠ guaranteed interoperability

== References ==
* ISO/IEC/IEEE 24765, systems and software engineering vocabulary, interoperability terminology.
* W3C Web Architecture, use of shared identifiers, protocols, and representations.
* IETF standards process and protocol specifications, for interoperable network implementations.
